# Store and check out every file exactly as it is on disk, byte for byte.
#
# Evidence records carry sha256 hashes of each other and of the configs and
# source files they were produced from, and those hashes were computed over the
# bytes on disk. If git rewrote line endings on checkout — which is what it does
# by default on Windows — a fresh clone would hold files whose hashes no longer
# match what the records say, and every provenance check in the repository would
# fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the research.
#
# So: no end-of-line conversion, anywhere, for anything.
* -text
